{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37"],"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"question":"zero-trust node sync field sign-off final project snapshot nominal latency handshake high latency timeout budget planning constraint","page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-18\\n\\n# Zero-Trust Node Sync: Handshake Prototype Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2018\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nThis note looks back at the first authenticated handshake prototype built 2026-08-06 for CIPH-34 (Zero-Trust Node Sync), ahead of multi-site local deployments.\\n\\n## What was prototyped\\n\\nA handshake in which each node presents a signed challenge/response before either side accepts replication traffic from the other. No central node is required to bootstrap trust between two peers.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-18\\n\\n# Zero-Trust Node Sync: Handshake Prototype Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2018\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nThis note looks back at the first authenticated handshake prototype built 2026-08-06 for CIPH-34 (Zero-Trust Node Sync), ahead of multi-site local deployments.\\n\\n## Result as of 2026-08-06\\n\\nThe handshake completed reliably across every run on a single LAN segment with nominal round-trip latency. No cross-node encryption mismatches or handshake rejections were seen at that stage.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-18\\n\\n# Zero-Trust Node Sync: Handshake Prototype Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2018\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nThis note looks back at the first authenticated handshake prototype built 2026-08-06 for CIPH-34 (Zero-Trust Node Sync), ahead of multi-site local deployments.\\n\\n## Open question\\n\\nThe prototype has only been exercised on one LAN segment. Whether the handshake holds up across a simulated multi-site link with realistic latency and jitter has not been tested and is the planned next step before this can support multi-site rollout.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 18 zero trust node sync handshak prototyp note owner bob document key doc 2018 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 this note look back at the first authent handshak prototyp built 2026 08 06 for ciph 34 zero trust node sync ahead of multi site local deploy what wa prototyp a handshak in which each node present a sign challeng respons befor either side accept replic traffic from the other no central node is requir to bootstrap trust between two peer sourc id src gdoc 18 zero trust node sync handshak prototyp note owner bob document key doc 2018 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 this note look back at the first authent handshak prototyp built 2026 08 06 for ciph 34 zero trust node sync ahead of multi site local deploy result a of 2026 08 06 the handshak complet reliabl across everi run on a singl lan segment with nomin round trip latenc no cross node encrypt mismatch or handshak reject were seen at that stage sourc id src gdoc 18 zero trust node sync handshak prototyp note owner bob document key doc 2018 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 this note look back at the first authent handshak prototyp built 2026 08 06 for ciph 34 zero trust node sync ahead of multi site local deploy open question the prototyp ha onli been exercis on one lan segment whether the handshak hold up across a simul multi site link with realist latenc and jitter ha not been test and is the plan next step befor this can support multi site rollout\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9dc21828a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Review.md\", \"id\": \"4c8ad9d86bb9e4c5\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3236820823917671, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11397058913109588, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8130089, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9dc21828a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1055, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:05\", \"token_count\": 453, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-38\\n\\n# Node Sync Handshake Prototype — Architecture Note\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2038\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nMulti-site local deployments need authenticated node sync without assuming a shared network password. T024 opened for a distributed zero-trust sync path; the first concrete deliverable was a replication handshake between peers.\\n\\n## Prototype (2026-08-06)\\n\\nBob implemented a node-replication handshake so each side must authenticate before accepting sync traffic from the other. That put an Active prototype on the board for T024.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-38\\n\\n# Node Sync Handshake Prototype — Architecture Note\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2038\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nMulti-site local deployments need authenticated node sync without assuming a shared network password. T024 opened for a distributed zero-trust sync path; the first concrete deliverable was a replication handshake between peers.\\n\\n## What this note does not claim\\n\\nNominal-latency validation and any later high-latency failure modes are outside this write-up. As of 2026-08-06 the task was Active on the strength of the prototype alone.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 38 node sync handshak prototyp architectur note owner bob document key doc 2038 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 multi site local deploy need authent node sync without assum a share network password t024 open for a distribut zero trust sync path the first concret deliver wa a replic handshak between peer prototyp 2026 08 06 bob implement a node replic handshak so each side must authent befor accept sync traffic from the other that put an activ prototyp on the board for t024 sourc id src gdoc 38 node sync handshak prototyp architectur note owner bob document key doc 2038 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 multi site local deploy need authent node sync without assum a share network password t024 open for a distribut zero trust sync path the first concret deliver wa a replic handshak between peer what this note doe not claim nomin latenc valid and ani later high latenc failur mode are outsid this write up a of 2026 08 06 the task wa activ on the strength of the prototyp alon\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9c5ca5e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Architecture-Review.md\", \"id\": \"1a260421319205d4\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3203966229826043, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1102941185465776, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8106358, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Architecture-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9c5ca5e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Architecture-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-15-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync-Architecture-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 825, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:21\", \"token_count\": 313, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-34\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Title**: Authenticated handshake for multi-site node sync\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nEnable distributed zero-trust node synchronization for multi-site local deployments, requiring an authenticated handshake between nodes. Validation of the handshake under high-latency networks failed with timeouts; the fix depends on the completed encryption work, but the task remains blocked pending resolution.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-34\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Title**: Authenticated handshake for multi-site node sync\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Authenticated node-replication handshake completes reliably between nodes.\\n\\n- Handshake succeeds under high-latency network conditions, not only nominal latency.\\n\\n- Blocking timeout issue is resolved before multi-site rollout can proceed.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-34\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Title**: Authenticated handshake for multi-site node sync\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nEnable distributed zero-trust node synchronization for multi-site local deployments, requiring an authenticated handshake between nodes. Validation of the handshake under high-latency networks failed with timeouts; the fix depends on the completed encryption work, but the task remains blocked pending resolution.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-34\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-34\\n\\n**Title**: Authenticated handshake for multi-site node sync\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-04**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because multi-site local deployments need distributed zero-trust node synchronization.*\\n\\n- **2026-09-22**: Diana - Handshake Timeout Block (Blocked)\\n\\n - *Blocked after validation showed handshake timeouts on high-latency networks; resolution depends on the encryption work but remains unresolved.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 34 sourc id src cu ciph 34 task id ciph 34 titl authent handshak for multi site node sync status block assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 08 04 descript enabl distribut zero trust node synchron for multi site local deploy requir an authent handshak between node valid of the handshak under high latenc network fail with timeout the fix depend on the complet encrypt work but the task remain block pend resolut clickup task ciph 34 sourc id src cu ciph 34 task id ciph 34 titl authent handshak for multi site node sync status block assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 08 04 accept criterion authent node replic handshak complet reliabl between node handshak succeed under high latenc network condit not onli nomin latenc block timeout issu is resolv befor multi site rollout can proceed clickup task ciph 34 sourc id src cu ciph 34 task id ciph 34 titl authent handshak for multi site node sync status block assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 08 04 descript enabl distribut zero trust node synchron for multi site local deploy requir an authent handshak between node valid of the handshak under high latenc network fail with timeout the fix depend on the complet encrypt work but the task remain block pend resolut clickup task ciph 34 sourc id src cu ciph 34 task id ciph 34 titl authent handshak for multi site node sync status block assigne bob prioriti high date creat 2026 08 04 activ histori 2026 08 04 alic task creat open open the task becaus multi site local deploy need distribut zero trust node synchron 2026 09 22 diana handshak timeout block block block after valid show handshak timeout on high latenc network resolut depend on the encrypt work but remain unresolv\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e993c5728a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-34-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync.md\", \"id\": \"d487d4d51c3b088f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.31932782239176705, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11397058913109584, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7984947, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-34-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e993c5728a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-34-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-34-Zero-Trust-Node-Sync.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1197, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:05\", \"token_count\": 534, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-27\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Node Sync Handshake Validation\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:04] Bob**: Ran the handshake validation under nominal latency — two nodes on the local network, dozens of connect attempts back to back. No failures.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:05] Evan**: Any dropped or retried handshakes at all?\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:30] Bob**: None. Every attempt authenticated cleanly on the first try at this latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:32] Diana**: We still need the high-latency case covered before this goes anywhere near the field.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:38] Bob**: Agreed, it's next on the list. First cut of the nominal-latency pass looks solid — leaving it in progress until we cover high latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:41] Diana**: Good.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 09:50] Diana**: Reopening this. Ran the handshake over a simulated high-latency link and it's timing out — never completes the exchange.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:08] Bob**: Timing out, or actively failing? Could just be the round trip budget being too tight.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:09] Diana**: Times out. And it gets worse the slower the link — feels like the handshake is doing more work per round trip than it should.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:18] Bob**: That tracks. The AES-256 pipeline we added on the output path adds per-packet overhead, and on a slow link that pushes the exchange past the timeout window. This depends on the encryption work settling down before we can retest — handshake work stays blocked for now.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 27 slack thread node sync handshak valid channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 08 last activ 2026 09 22 2026 08 08 09 04 bob ran the handshak valid under nomin latenc two node on the local network dozen of connect attempt back to back no failur 2026 08 08 09 05 evan ani drop or retri handshak at all 2026 08 08 09 30 bob none everi attempt authent clean on the first tri at this latenc 2026 08 08 09 32 diana we still need the high latenc case cover befor this go anywher near the field 2026 08 08 09 38 bob agre it s next on the list first cut of the nomin latenc pas look solid leav it in progress until we cover high latenc 2026 08 08 09 41 diana good 2026 09 22 09 50 diana reopen this ran the handshak over a simul high latenc link and it s time out never complet the exchang 2026 09 22 10 08 bob time out or activ fail could just be the round trip budget be too tight 2026 09 22 10 09 diana time out and it get wors the slower the link feel like the handshak is do more work per round trip than it should 2026 09 22 1018 bob that track the ae 256 pipelin we ad on the output path add per packet overhead and on a slow link that push the exchang past the timeout window this depend on the encrypt work settl down befor we can retest handshak work stay block for now\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e92703ba8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"id\": \"7c000945298cb210\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3071333453459531, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09558823620850447, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8007386, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e92703ba8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1559, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:36\", \"token_count\": 450, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-26\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Node Sync Handshake Prototype\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-06\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:30] Bob**: Starting on the replication handshake for the zero-trust node sync. First requirement is that two nodes have to authenticate each other before either one accepts replicated entries.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:37] Evan**: How's a node proving who it is right now?\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:38] Bob**: Each node has a registered identity it presents at connect time. If the peer doesn't recognize it, the connection gets dropped before any data moves.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 09:49] Charlie**: Does the handshake add noticeable overhead to the redaction jobs running on the same box?\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 10:40] Bob**: Negligible so far — it's a short exchange before the sync session opens, nothing that touches the active redaction path.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 10:41] Diana**: What's next after the prototype?\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 11:47] Bob**: Need to check it holds up under real network delay, not just on my two test nodes on the same switch. That's the next pass.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 26 slack thread node sync handshak prototyp channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 06 2026 08 06 09 30 bob start on the replic handshak for the zero trust node sync first requir is that two node have to authent each other befor either one accept replic entri 2026 08 06 09 37 evan how s a node prove who it is right now 2026 08 06 09 38 bob each node ha a regist ident it present at connect time if the peer doesn t recogn it the connect get drop befor ani data move 2026 08 06 09 49 charli doe the handshak add notic overhead to the redact job run on the same box 2026 08 06 10 40 bob neglig so far it s a short exchang befor the sync session open noth that touch the activ redact path 2026 08 06 10 41 diana what s next after the prototyp 2026 08 06 11 47 bob need to check it hold up under real network delay not just on my two test node on the same switch that s the next pas\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8f020a28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"id\": \"6657f131b0d26923\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2855440310726508, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.06617647153235831, \"vector_similarity\": 0.79740167, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8f020a28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-06-node-sync-handshake-prototype.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1079, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:24\", \"token_count\": 317, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nDiana walked the high-latency handshake timeout. The team left handshake work blocked; no timeout-bump workaround. Path still depends on the encryption workstream.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Diana**: Handshake triage — nominal latency was fine; Bob's earlier validation held up on the local network. On a simulated high-latency link the handshake never finishes. It times out.\\n\\n**Bob**: That matches what I expected once we left the happy path. The prototype assumed round trips stay quick. High latency breaks the exchange.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Is this an encryption cost problem? AES-256 on the wire path is in the dependency chain here.\\n\\n**Bob**: It's related. The handshake still has to complete under that load, and on a slow link it doesn't. I don't have a fix that keeps the current exchange as-is.\\n\\n**Evan**: Bumping timeouts just hides it. If the link is slow enough, we still fail.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll leave the high-latency repro in place so we can re-check when encryption or the handshake design changes.\\n\\n**Alice**: Then we leave it. Handshake work stays blocked on timeouts under high latency. It depends on the encryption path, and we're not inventing a workaround in this meeting.\\n\\n**Bob**: Agreed — no timeout bump. We'll revisit when the crypto path moves.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari diana walk the high latenc handshak timeout the team left handshak work block no timeout bump workaround path still depend on the encrypt workstream sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript diana handshak triag nomin latenc wa fine bob s earlier valid held up on the local network on a simul high latenc link the handshak never finish it time out bob that match what i expect onc we left the happi path the prototyp assum round trip stay quick high latenc break the exchang charli is this an encrypt cost problem ae 256 on the wire path is in the depend chain here bob it s relat the handshak still ha to complet under that load and on a slow link it doesn t i don t have a fix that keep the current exchang ais evan bump timeout just hide it if the link is slow enough we still fail diana i ll leav the high latenc repro in place so we can re check when encrypt or the handshak design chang alic then we leav it handshak work stay block on timeout under high latenc it depend on the encrypt path and we re not invent a workaround in this meet bob agre no timeout bump we ll revisit when the crypto path move\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"id\": \"edcdc1df7188b1a3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2823401188909764, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07352941270139485, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7695651, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1463, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:18\", \"token_count\": 417, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-12\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Batch Failure Strategy (Fail-Closed)\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-12\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-07-16\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:09] Bob**: For the batch fail-closed question, we need to decide what happens if the engine crashes halfway through a 1,000-file batch. Do we keep the successful ones?\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:26] Charlie**: Absolutely not. If we can't guarantee 100% of the batch is safe, we should fail-closed. No partial exports.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:28] Bob**: Agreed. Drafting the plan now. If any worker node throws an unhandled exception, we abort the entire job and purge the output buffer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:43] Charlie**: I've added an exception hook to the core engine. It catches low-level segfaults and signals the controller to stop all active streams.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 11:23] Bob**: Implementation complete. Added an atomic rename step at the very end — the output folder stays empty until the last file is verified.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 12:53] Diana**: What about logs? We need to know *why* it failed.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:16] Bob**: Crash report gets written to a separate `audit_log.json` before the shutdown. Captures the stack trace and the filename that triggered the fault.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:17] Charlie**: Perfect. :lock:\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:19] Alice**: Thanks.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:30] Diana**: QA pass on fail-closed is done — confirmed no output file gets written on failure and the temp files get securely deleted. Signing off before the encryption and offline work start relying on this.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:31] Bob**: Calling this done.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 12 slack thread batch failur strategi fail close channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 12 last activ 2026 07 16 2026 06 12 10 09 bob for the batch fail close question we need to decid what happen if the engin crash halfway through a1 000 file batch do we keep the success one 2026 06 12 10 26 charli absolut not if we can t guarante 100 of the batch is safe we should fail close no partial export 2026 06 12 10 28 bob agre draft the plan now if ani worker node throw an unhandl except we abort the entir job and purg the output buffer 2026 06 12 10 43 charli i ve ad an except hook to the core engin it catch low level segfault and signal the control to stop all activ stream 2026 06 12 11 23 bob implement complet ad an atom renam step at the veri end the output folder stay empti until the last file is verifi 2026 06 12 12 53 diana what about log we need to know whi it fail 2026 06 12 13 16 bob crash report get written to a separ audit _ log json befor the shutdown captur the stack trace and the filenam that trigger the fault 2026 06 12 13 17 charli perfect lock 2026 06 12 13 19 alic thank 2026 07 16 09 30 diana qa pas on fail close is done confirm no output file get written on failur and the temp file get secur delet sign off befor the encrypt and offlin work start reli on this 2026 07 16 09 31 bob call this done\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e906ce748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"id\": \"1313e24c5f4d4803\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24888950184516243, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.0551470597788035, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7009552, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e906ce748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1616, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:03\", \"token_count\": 478, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-07\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Weekly Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-05\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nBob reported offline-auth rotation cannot complete without network access — left blocked. Evan's disk-usage monitor loop is in; Diana's halt-behavior sign-off still pending.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-07\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Weekly Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-05\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Bob**: Offline-auth mock first — not well. I built the local mock and ran the rotation flow with the network denied. Rotation can't complete offline.\\n\\n**Diana**: Is that a bug in the mock, or the design?\\n\\n**Bob**: The design. The flow we picked assumes a connection to finish rotation. I don't have a fix yet — we should call it blocked.\\n\\n**Alice**: Agreed. Offline auth stays blocked until we have an offline-capable rotation approach. Evan, status on the disk-usage monitor?\\n\\n**Evan**: Monitor loop is in. It watches disk usage so we can enforce the quota policy. Haven't had Diana sign off on the halt behavior yet.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Has anyone verified the halt behavior yet?\\n\\n**Evan**: Not signed off. Monitor is in progress; Diana still needs to confirm it actually stops writes at the configured quota.\\n\\n**Evan**: I'll wait on Diana's halt sign-off before calling quota monitoring done.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 07 firefli transcript week sync date 2026 08 05 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari bob report offlin auth rotat can not complet without network access left block evan s disk usag monitor loop is in diana s halt behavior sign off still pend sourc id src meet 07 firefli transcript week sync date 2026 08 05 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript bob offlin auth mock first not well i built the local mock and ran the rotat flow with the network deni rotat can t complet offlin diana is that a bug in the mock or the design bob the design the flow we pick assum a connect to finish rotat i don t have a fix yet we should call it block alic agre offlin auth stay block until we have an offlin capabl rotat approach evan status on the disk usag monitor evan monitor loop is in it watch disk usag so we can enforc the quota polici haven t had diana sign off on the halt behavior yet charli ha anyon verifi the halt behavior yet evan not sign off monitor is in progress diana still need to confirm it actual stop write at the configur quota evan i ll wait on diana s halt sign off befor call quota monitor done\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e94820e08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-05-Weekly-Sync.md\", \"id\": \"0d85de036037cfcd\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24757569220851128, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.040441177440730405, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73088956, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-05-Weekly-Sync.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e94820e08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-05-Weekly-Sync.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-05-Weekly-Sync.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1273, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:13\", \"token_count\": 368, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \" - *Opened the task because the strict offline air-gapped mode must be testable.*\\n\\n- **2026-08-10**: Diana - Offline Sign-off (Completed)\\n\\n - *Signed off on the offline batch run, depending on the completed AES-256 encryption pipeline, noting a 45-second remote licence-check hang; sign-off recorded as preliminary only, not a compliance certification.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"open the task becaus the strict offlin air gap mode must be testabl 2026 08 10 diana offlin sign off complet sign off on the offlin batch run depend on the complet ae 256 encrypt pipelin note a 45 second remot licenc check hang sign off record a preliminari onli not a complianc certif\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e969dcb28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-37-Air-Gapped-Mode-Testing.md\", \"id\": \"b6b76363ffc0abba\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.23605959657186013, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.025735295102657322, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7268163, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-37-Air-Gapped-Mode-Testing.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e969dcb28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-37-Air-Gapped-Mode-Testing.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-37-Air-Gapped-Mode-Testing.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1365, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:41\", \"token_count\": 610, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-47\\n\\n# Sign-off Note: Offline Batch Run (Preliminary)\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2047\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n## What Was Run\\n\\nA full batch redaction run was executed under the offline test harness (T027) with network access denied, using a local sample document set. The run depended on the completed AES-256 at-rest encryption pipeline (T021), since offline output still needs to be encrypted without any network-based key service.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-47\\n\\n# Sign-off Note: Offline Batch Run (Preliminary)\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2047\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n## Result\\n\\nThe batch completed successfully end-to-end with the network denied: no network-dependent call blocked the run, and local policy parsing worked entirely from bundled definitions.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-47\\n\\n# Sign-off Note: Offline Batch Run (Preliminary)\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2047\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n## Noted Issue: 45-Second Licence-Check Hang\\n\\nThe run was not clean — the HTTP client attempted to verify the license key against a remote server before timing out and falling back to the cached local license, adding roughly 45 seconds of startup delay. This is logged as a known issue, not something this sign-off waives.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-47\\n\\n# Sign-off Note: Offline Batch Run (Preliminary)\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2047\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n## Scope of This Sign-off\\n\\nThis sign-off is **preliminary** and covers functional completion of a batch run offline only. It is explicitly **not** a compliance certification — it does not cover side-channel analysis, physical security, or any regulatory attestation. No patient records or clinical data were used in this test run.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 47 sign off note offlin batch run preliminari owner diana document key doc 2047 last updat 2026 08 10 what wa run a full batch redact run wa execut under the offlin test har t027 with network access deni use a local sampl document set the run depend on the complet ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin t021 sinc offlin output still need to be encrypt without ani network base key servic sourc id src gdoc 47 sign off note offlin batch run preliminari owner diana document key doc 2047 last updat 2026 08 10 result the batch complet success end to end with the network deni no network depend call block the run and local polici pars work entir from bundl definit sourc id src gdoc 47 sign off note offlin batch run preliminari owner diana document key doc 2047 last updat 2026 08 10 note issu 45 second licenc check hang the run wa not clean the http client attempt to verifi the licens key against a remot server befor time out and fall back to the cach local licens ad rough 45 second of startup delay this is log a a known issu not someth this sign off waif sourc id src gdoc 47 sign off note offlin batch run preliminari owner diana document key doc 2047 last updat 2026 08 10 scope of this sign off this sign off is preliminari and cover function complet of a batch run offlin onli it is explicit not a complianc certif it doe not cover side channel analysi physic secur or ani regulatori attest no patient record or clinic data were use in this test run\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9b0c0dc8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-10-Air-Gapped-Mode-Offline-Signoff.md\", \"id\": \"5b05fa1d83b734fd\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2351669953901857, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.03308823627169386, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7066841, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-10-Air-Gapped-Mode-Offline-Signoff.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9b0c0dc8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-10-Air-Gapped-Mode-Offline-Signoff.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-10-Air-Gapped-Mode-Offline-Signoff.md\", \"t