{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37"],"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"question":"CIPH-34 final project snapshot field sign-off high-latency constraint timeout budget planning","page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-18\\n\\n# Zero-Trust Node Sync: Handshake Prototype Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2018\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nThis note looks back at the first authenticated handshake prototype built 2026-08-06 for CIPH-34 (Zero-Trust Node Sync), ahead of multi-site local deployments.\\n\\n## What was prototyped\\n\\nA handshake in which each node presents a signed challenge/response before either side accepts replication traffic from the other. No central node is required to bootstrap trust between two peers.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-18\\n\\n# Zero-Trust Node Sync: Handshake Prototype Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2018\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nThis note looks back at the first authenticated handshake prototype built 2026-08-06 for CIPH-34 (Zero-Trust Node Sync), ahead of multi-site local deployments.\\n\\n## Result as of 2026-08-06\\n\\nThe handshake completed reliably across every run on a single LAN segment with nominal round-trip latency. No cross-node encryption mismatches or handshake rejections were seen at that stage.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-18\\n\\n# Zero-Trust Node Sync: Handshake Prototype Notes\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2018\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-15 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-06)\\n\\nThis note looks back at the first authenticated handshake prototype built 2026-08-06 for CIPH-34 (Zero-Trust Node Sync), ahead of multi-site local deployments.\\n\\n## Open question\\n\\nThe prototype has only been exercised on one LAN segment. Whether the handshake holds up across a simulated multi-site link with realistic latency and jitter has not been tested and is the planned next step before this can support multi-site rollout.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 18 zero trust node sync handshak prototyp note owner bob document key doc 2018 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 this note look back at the first authent handshak prototyp built 2026 08 06 for ciph 34 zero trust node sync ahead of multi site local deploy what wa prototyp a handshak in which each node present a sign challeng respons befor either side accept replic traffic from the other no central node is requir to bootstrap trust between two peer sourc id src gdoc 18 zero trust node sync handshak prototyp note owner bob document key doc 2018 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 this note look back at the first authent handshak prototyp built 2026 08 06 for ciph 34 zero trust node sync ahead of multi site local deploy result a of 2026 08 06 the handshak complet reliabl across everi run on a singl lan segment with nomin round trip latenc no cross node encrypt mismatch or handshak reject were seen at that stage sourc id src gdoc 18 zero trust node sync handshak prototyp note owner bob document key doc 2018 last updat 2026 08 15 retrospect cover 2026 08 06 this note look back at the first authent handshak prototyp built 2026 08 06 for ciph 34 zero trust node sync ahead of multi site local deploy open question the prototyp ha onli been exercis on one lan segment whether the handshak hold up across a simul multi site link with realist latenc and jitter ha not been test and is the plan next step befor this can support multi site rollout\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7