1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:13\", \"token_count\": 524, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nDiana walked the high-latency handshake timeout. The team left handshake work blocked; no timeout-bump workaround. Path still depends on the encryption workstream.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-11\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Handshake Protocol Deep Dive\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Diana**: Handshake triage — nominal latency was fine; Bob's earlier validation held up on the local network. On a simulated high-latency link the handshake never finishes. It times out.\\n\\n**Bob**: That matches what I expected once we left the happy path. The prototype assumed round trips stay quick. High latency breaks the exchange.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Is this an encryption cost problem? AES-256 on the wire path is in the dependency chain here.\\n\\n**Bob**: It's related. The handshake still has to complete under that load, and on a slow link it doesn't. I don't have a fix that keeps the current exchange as-is.\\n\\n**Evan**: Bumping timeouts just hides it. If the link is slow enough, we still fail.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll leave the high-latency repro in place so we can re-check when encryption or the handshake design changes.\\n\\n**Alice**: Then we leave it. Handshake work stays blocked on timeouts under high latency. It depends on the encryption path, and we're not inventing a workaround in this meeting.\\n\\n**Bob**: Agreed — no timeout bump. We'll revisit when the crypto path moves.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari diana walk the high latenc handshak timeout the team left handshak work block no timeout bump workaround path still depend on the encrypt workstream sourc id src meet 11 firefli transcript handshak protocol deep dive date 2026 09 22 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript diana handshak triag nomin latenc wa fine bob s earlier valid held up on the local network on a simul high latenc link the handshak never finish it time out bob that match what i expect onc we left the happi path the prototyp assum round trip stay quick high latenc break the exchang charli is this an encrypt cost problem ae 256 on the wire path is in the depend chain here bob it s relat the handshak still ha to complet under that load and on a slow link it doesn t i don t have a fix that keep the current exchang ais evan bump timeout just hide it if the link is slow enough we still fail diana i ll leav the high latenc repro in place so we can re check when encrypt or the handshak design chang alic then we leav it handshak work stay block on timeout under high latenc it depend on the encrypt path and we re not invent a workaround in this meet bob agre no timeout bump we ll revisit when the crypto path move\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"id\": \"edcdc1df7188b1a3\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2556983206940615, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.05119775813437365, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7328663, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e940b5088a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-09-22-Handshake-Protocol-Deep-Dive.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1463, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:18\", \"token_count\": 417, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-27\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Node Sync Handshake Validation\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-08-08\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-22\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:04] Bob**: Ran the handshake validation under nominal latency — two nodes on the local network, dozens of connect attempts back to back. No failures.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:05] Evan**: Any dropped or retried handshakes at all?\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:30] Bob**: None. Every attempt authenticated cleanly on the first try at this latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:32] Diana**: We still need the high-latency case covered before this goes anywhere near the field.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:38] Bob**: Agreed, it's next on the list. First cut of the nominal-latency pass looks solid — leaving it in progress until we cover high latency.\\n\\n**[2026-08-08 09:41] Diana**: Good.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 09:50] Diana**: Reopening this. Ran the handshake over a simulated high-latency link and it's timing out — never completes the exchange.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:08] Bob**: Timing out, or actively failing? Could just be the round trip budget being too tight.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:09] Diana**: Times out. And it gets worse the slower the link — feels like the handshake is doing more work per round trip than it should.\\n\\n**[2026-09-22 10:18] Bob**: That tracks. The AES-256 pipeline we added on the output path adds per-packet overhead, and on a slow link that pushes the exchange past the timeout window. This depends on the encryption work settling down before we can retest — handshake work stays blocked for now.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 27 slack thread node sync handshak valid channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 08 last activ 2026 09 22 2026 08 08 09 04 bob ran the handshak valid under nomin latenc two node on the local network dozen of connect attempt back to back no failur 2026 08 08 09 05 evan ani drop or retri handshak at all 2026 08 08 09 30 bob none everi attempt authent clean on the first tri at this latenc 2026 08 08 09 32 diana we still need the high latenc case cover befor this go anywher near the field 2026 08 08 09 38 bob agre it s next on the list first cut of the nomin latenc pas look solid leav it in progress until we cover high latenc 2026 08 08 09 41 diana good 2026 09 22 09 50 diana reopen this ran the handshak over a simul high latenc link and it s time out never complet the exchang 2026 09 22 10 08 bob time out or activ fail could just be the round trip budget be too tight 2026 09 22 10 09 diana time out and it get wors the slower the link feel like the handshak is do more work per round trip than it should 2026 09 22 1018 bob that track the ae 256 pipelin we ad on the output path add per packet overhead and on a slow link that push the exchang past the timeout window this depend on the encrypt work settl down befor we can retest handshak work stay block for now\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e92703ba8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"id\": \"7c000945298cb210\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2530718296031533, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.046543416575933264, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73497146, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e92703ba8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-08-node-sync-handshake-validation.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1559, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:36\", \"token_count\": 450, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-47\\n\\n# Sign-off Note: Offline Batch Run (Preliminary)\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2047\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n## What Was Run\\n\\nA full batch redaction run was executed under the offline test harness (T027) with network access denied, using a local sample document set. The run depended on the completed AES-256 at-rest encryption pipeline (T021), since offline output still needs to be encrypted without any network-based key service.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-47\\n\\n# Sign-off Note: Offline Batch Run (Preliminary)\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2047\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n## Result\\n\\nThe batch completed successfully end-to-end with the network denied: no network-dependent call blocked the run, and local policy parsing worked entirely from bundled definitions.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-47\\n\\n# Sign-off Note: Offline Batch Run (Preliminary)\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2047\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n## Noted Issue: 45-Second Licence-Check Hang\\n\\nThe run was not clean — the HTTP client attempted to verify the license key against a remote server before timing out and falling back to the cached local license, adding roughly 45 seconds of startup delay. This is logged as a known issue, not something this sign-off waives.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-47\\n\\n# Sign-off Note: Offline Batch Run (Preliminary)\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2047\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n## Scope of This Sign-off\\n\\nThis sign-off is **preliminary** and covers functional completion of a batch run offline only. It is explicitly **not** a compliance certification — it does not cover side-channel analysis, physical security, or any regulatory attestation. No patient records or clinical data were used in this test run.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 47 sign off note offlin batch run preliminari owner diana document key doc 2047 last updat 2026 08 10 what wa run a full batch redact run wa execut under the offlin test har t027 with network access deni use a local sampl document set the run depend on the complet ae 256 at rest encrypt pipelin t021 sinc offlin output still need to be encrypt without ani network base key servic sourc id src gdoc 47 sign off note offlin batch run preliminari owner diana document key doc 2047 last updat 2026 08 10 result the batch complet success end to end with the network deni no network depend call block the run and local polici pars work entir from bundl definit sourc id src gdoc 47 sign off note offlin batch run preliminari owner diana document key doc 2047 last updat 2026 08 10 note issu 45 second licenc check hang the run wa not clean the http client attempt to verifi the licens key against a remot server befor time out and fall back to the cach local licens ad rough 45 second of startup delay this is log a a known issu not someth this sign off waif sourc id src gdoc 47 sign off note offlin batch run preliminari owner diana document key doc 2047 last updat 2026 08 10 scope of this sign off this sign off is preliminari and cover function complet of a batch run offlin onli it is explicit not a complianc certif it doe not cover side channel analysi physic secur or ani regulatori attest no patient record or clinic data were use in this test run\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9b0c0dc8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-10-Air-Gapped-Mode-Offline-Signoff.md\", \"id\": \"5b05fa1d83b734fd\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24972127351224502, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.04188907501749288, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73466307, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-10-Air-Gapped-Mode-Offline-Signoff.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9b0c0dc8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-10-Air-Gapped-Mode-Offline-Signoff.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-10-Air-Gapped-Mode-Offline-Signoff.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1322, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:40\", \"token_count\": 456, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-07\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Weekly Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-05\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nBob reported offline-auth rotation cannot complete without network access — left blocked. Evan's disk-usage monitor loop is in; Diana's halt-behavior sign-off still pending.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-07\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: Weekly Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-05\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Bob**: Offline-auth mock first — not well. I built the local mock and ran the rotation flow with the network denied. Rotation can't complete offline.\\n\\n**Diana**: Is that a bug in the mock, or the design?\\n\\n**Bob**: The design. The flow we picked assumes a connection to finish rotation. I don't have a fix yet — we should call it blocked.\\n\\n**Alice**: Agreed. Offline auth stays blocked until we have an offline-capable rotation approach. Evan, status on the disk-usage monitor?\\n\\n**Evan**: Monitor loop is in. It watches disk usage so we can enforce the quota policy. Haven't had Diana sign off on the halt behavior yet.\\n\\n**Charlie**: Has anyone verified the halt behavior yet?\\n\\n**Evan**: Not signed off. Monitor is in progress; Diana still needs to confirm it actually stops writes at the configured quota.\\n\\n**Evan**: I'll wait on Diana's halt sign-off before calling quota monitoring done.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 07 firefli transcript week sync date 2026 08 05 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari bob report offlin auth rotat can not complet without network access left block evan s disk usag monitor loop is in diana s halt behavior sign off still pend sourc id src meet 07 firefli transcript week sync date 2026 08 05 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript bob offlin auth mock first not well i built the local mock and ran the rotat flow with the network deni rotat can t complet offlin diana is that a bug in the mock or the design bob the design the flow we pick assum a connect to finish rotat i don t have a fix yet we should call it block alic agre offlin auth stay block until we have an offlin capabl rotat approach evan status on the disk usag monitor evan monitor loop is in it watch disk usag so we can enforc the quota polici haven t had diana sign off on the halt behavior yet charli ha anyon verifi the halt behavior yet evan not sign off monitor is in progress diana still need to confirm it actual stop write at the configur quota evan i ll wait on diana s halt sign off befor call quota monitor done\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e94820e08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-05-Weekly-Sync.md\", \"id\": \"0d85de036037cfcd\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24833469751224502, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.04188907501749288, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73004115, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-05-Weekly-Sync.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e94820e08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-05-Weekly-Sync.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-08-05-Weekly-Sync.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1273, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:13\", \"token_count\": 368, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"CIPH-34 final project snapshot field sign-off high-latency constraint timeout budget planning\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"No. The nominal-latency pass was explicitly insufficient for field sign-off; the handshake had to succeed under high-latency conditions as well. That validation now fails—timeouts worsen as links slow—so CIPH-34 remains blocked. [SRC-CU-CIPH-34; SRC-SLACK-27]\n\nPlanning should assume **no approved timeout-extension budget**. The team rejected a timeout bump as a workaround because sufficiently slow links would still fail; the required constraint is a proven high-latency handshake under the encryption-path load, pending redesign/encryption changes and retest. [SRC-MEET-11]"}}
